                <pb facs="0349" n="259" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg259"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6211/479: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Commissioner at Berlin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dresel</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-18T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 18, 1920—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>515. Referring to your telegram no. 588, June 8.</p>
                <p>Department believes the present would be an unfortunate time to raise the
                    question of unofficial representation of Germany in the United States, and
                    leaves to your discretion the best way of bringing this viewpoint to the German
                    Government’s attention to the end that public and official discussion of the
                    question may be avoided.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
